# The Pass — Cursor rules

Read `AGENTS.md`, `docs/GROK_HANDOFF.md`, and the active ExecPlan before editing.

## Scope lock

- Build one resettable disruption: the fryer becomes unavailable for 12 minutes.
- Use exactly four stations and the six seeded tickets until the canonical journey passes.
- The clock must continue while the agent reasons.
- The human UI and WebMCP tools must mutate the same store.
- The page validates atomic agent actions. It does not expose a magic optimizer.
- A human-only approval commits a staged recovery.
- Do not add auth, a backend, real POS integration, multiple scenarios, settings, or generative AI inside the app.

## Working style

- Make the smallest vertical change and validate it before continuing.
- Keep product logic framework-free under `src/domain/`.
- Keep browser API code under `src/webmcp/`.
- Do not let React components contain scheduling or version-validation logic.
- Add or update tests whenever behavior changes.
- Preserve the industrial KDS visual direction in `docs/DESIGN_DIRECTION.md`.
- Update `docs/EXEC_PLAN.md` as implementation discoveries are made.

## Required commands before claiming completion

```bash
npm run check
npm run test
npm run test:e2e
npm run build
```

Report the exact command result. Never say a check passed unless it was run.
